an, IT Helpdesk Officer, Digital Entrepreneur"},{id:"tailoring",name:"Tailoring & Fashion Designing",category:"Textiles & Design",description:"Garment construction, pattern cutting and creative fashion design for entrepreneurship and industry.",image:"/images/courses/tailoring.jpg",icon:"tailoring",fullDescription:"Master the art and business of fashion through our comprehensive tailoring and design programme. Learn pattern cutting, garment construction, fitting techniques, and fashion design principles. Students develop entrepreneurial skills to launch their own tailoring or design businesses while meeting industry standards for quality and innovation.",duration:"12 months (Full-time)",entryRequirements:["Secondary School Certificate (MSCE) or equivalent","Artistic aptitude or interest in fashion & fabric craft","Basic sewing skills welcomed though not mandatory"],learningOutcomes:["Create accurate patterns and grade garments for different sizes","Construct high-quality garments using industrial sewing machinery","Design original fashion collections and contemporary African wear","Understand fabric properties and material selection","Develop business, costing and tailoring shop entrepreneurship skills"],careerPath:"Fashion Designer, Master Tailor, Clothing Entrepreneur, Quality Controller, Fashion Consultant"},{id:"electrical",name:"Electrical Installation & Electronics",category:"Electrical & Energy",description:"Safe wiring practices, domestic and commercial installation, and core electronics principles.",image:"/images/courses/electrical.jpg",icon:"electrical",fullDescription:"A comprehensive course in electrical installation combining safety practices with practical skills. Students learn to design, install, and maintain electrical systems for residential and commercial properties. The programme includes electronics principles, troubleshooting techniques, and compliance with national electrical codes.",duration:"12 months (Full-time)",entryRequirements:["Secondary School Certificate (MSCE) or equivalent","Pass in Physical Science / Physics & Mathematics","Good physical fitness for workshop & field installations"],learningOutcomes:["Design safe electrical installations for homes and businesses","Install and test conduit wiring systems and main distribution switchboards","Diagnose and repair electrical circuitry faults with precision multimeters","Understand and apply national electrical safety codes & regulations","Install renewable energy systems including solar PV panels and inverters"],careerPath:"Licensed Electrician, Electrical Installation Technician, Solar PV Installer, Site Supervisor, Electrical Contractor"},{id:"carpentry",name:"Carpentry & Joinery",category:"Construction & Building",description:"Timber work, furniture making and joinery techniques for construction and bespoke craftsmanship.",image:"/images/courses/carpentry.jpg",icon:"carpentry",fullDescription:"Learn traditional and modern carpentry techniques to build and repair structures and furniture. This course covers wood selection, joinery methods, finishing techniques, and custom furniture design. Students work on real projects and develop skills in both residential construction and artisanal craftsmanship.",duration:"12 months (Full-time)",entryRequirements:["Secondary School Certificate (MSCE) or equivalent","Mechanical aptitude and attention to structural measurement","Good hand-eye coordination"],learningOutcomes:["Select and season timber materials appropriately","Execute mortise, tenon, and modern joinery techniques","Construct doors, window frames, and roofing timber trusses","Design and hand-craft custom wooden furniture","Apply professional protective varnishes, stains, and wood finishes"],careerPath:"Master Carpenter, Furniture Maker, Construction Timber Supervisor, Wood Craftsperson, Joinery Entrepreneur"},{id:"bricklaying",name:"Bricklaying",category:"Construction & Building",description:"Masonry, concrete work and structural building practices essential to the construction industry.",image:"/images/courses/bricklaying.jpg",icon:"bricklaying",fullDescription:"Master the essential skills of masonry and structural building. Students learn bricklaying, blockwork, concrete work, and restoration techniques. This course prepares graduates for employment on construction sites and capacity to manage small building projects independently.",duration:"12 months (Full-time)",entryRequirements:["Secondary School Certificate (MSCE) or equivalent","Physical fitness for construction yard practical work","Practical problem-solving ability"],learningOutcomes:["Lay bricks, stones and blocks to professional plumb and level standards","Prepare, mix and cast reinforced concrete foundations and lintels","Read, interpret and scale architectural building construction blueprints","Implement site occupational health and safety standards","Manage small construction sites and estimate building materials accurately"],careerPath:"Certified Builder, Masonry Contractor, Construction Site Supervisor, Building Inspector"},{id:"welding",name:"Fabrication & Welding",category:"Engineering & Mechanics",description:"Metal fabrication, arc and gas welding techniques for durable, in-demand craft skills.",image:"/images/courses/welding.jpg",icon:"welding",fullDescription:"Develop expertise in metal fabrication and welding through hands-on training in modern welding techniques. Students learn arc welding, gas welding, metal cutting, and structural fabrication. This high-demand skill prepares graduates for roles in construction, manufacturing, and infrastructure development.",duration:"12 months (Full-time)",entryRequirements:["Secondary School Certificate (MSCE) or equivalent","Good physical health and visual acuity","Commitment to workshop safety protocols"],learningOutcomes:["Perform manual metal arc (MMA) and oxy-acetylene welding to industry standard","Cut, bend, and prepare structural metals for welding fabrication","Fabricate security gates, window burglar bars, roof trusses, and steel tanks","Read welding engineering drawings and technical joint specifications","Apply strict workshop eye and fire safety procedures"],careerPath:"Certified Welder, Structural Steel Fabricator, Metalwork Contractor, Industrial Maintenance Welder"},{id:"plumbing",name:"Plumbing",category:"Construction & Building",description:"Water systems, pipe fitting and sanitation solutions for residential and commercial projects.",image:"/images/courses/plumbing.jpg",icon:"plumbing",fullDescription:"Comprehensive training in plumbing systems for residential and commercial applications. Students master water distribution systems, drainage, sanitation solutions, and pipe fitting techniques. The course emphasizes safety, efficiency, and environmental responsibility in plumbing practice.",duration:"12 months (Full-time)",entryRequirements:["Secondary School Certificate (MSCE) or equivalent","Practical spatial reasoning and problem-solving skills","Comfort working in varied domestic and commercial environments"],learningOutcomes:["Design and install pressurised domestic clean water supply networks","Install sanitary fixtures, drainage traps, waste pipes and soakaway systems","Work proficiently with PVC, PPR, copper, and galvanized iron piping","Implement plumbing and municipal public health safety codes","Diagnose leaks, blockages, pressure drops and execute rapid repairs"],careerPath:"Licensed Plumber, Water Utility Technician, Plumbing & Sanitation Contractor"},{id:"automobile",name:"Automobile Mechanics",category:"Engineering & Mechanics",description:"Engine systems, vehicle servicing and diagnostics to launch a career in the motor trade.",image:"/images/courses/automobile.jpg",icon:"automobile",fullDescription:"Become a skilled automotive technician through comprehensive training in vehicle mechanics and diagnostics. Students learn engine systems, transmission, electrical systems, and modern diagnostic techniques. This course prepares graduates for the growing automotive industry and entrepreneurial opportunities.",duration:"12 months (Full-time)",entryRequirements:["Secondary School Certificate (MSCE) or equivalent","Keen interest in mechanical systems and vehicles","Basic analytical and problem-solving skills"],learningOutcomes:["Disassemble, overhaul, service, and tune internal combustion engines","Diagnose automotive electrical, starter, alternator, and lighting circuits","Service braking systems, manual and automatic transmissions, and suspension","Operate computerized vehicle diagnostic scanners and interpret trouble codes","Conduct roadworthiness safety inspections to national transport standards"],careerPath:"Automotive Mechanic, Garage Workshop Foreman, Vehicle Diagnostic Specialist, Auto Parts Entrepreneur"}],wa={mission:"To provide relevant technical education and training to support student goals, a skilled workforce and the economic vitality of our communities.",vision:"Excellent leading institution in our community, recognized for our commitment to excellence in technical education.",values:["Transparency and Accountability","Collaboration and teamwork","Excellence and Creativity","Accessibility","Integrity","Innovativeness","Community Engagement","Lifelong learning","Student centeredness","Continuous improvement"],history:"Aida Chilembwe Community Technical College is located near the Providence Industrial Mission (PIM) site in Chiradzulu district, Malawi. Conceived in response to the need for a skilled workforce, the college empowers individuals and transforms communities through technical and vocational education. It is named in honour of Aida Chilembwe, the wife of social activist Reverend John Chilembwe. Aida was an artisan skilled in tailoring, cookery, and brick making, and her dedication to craftsmanship and community service continues to inspire the college. The college was officially opened on 13 September 2018 by His Excellency the former President of Malawi, Professor Arthur Peter Mutharika. It began with eight programmes: Automobile Mechanics, Bricklaying, Carpentry and Joinery, Information and Communication Technology, Electrical Installation and Electronics, Fabrication and Welding, Plumbing, and Textile and Fashion Designing. The college operates under the Directorate of Technical and Vocational Training in the Ministry of Labour.",motto:"Where knowledge meets opportunities",openedOn:"13 September 2018",location:"Near Providence Industrial Mission (PIM), Chiradzulu district, Malawi",oversight:"Directorate of Technical and Vocational Training, Ministry of Labour",facilities:["Well-equipped ICT laboratory with modern computers and networking equipment","Fully stocked tailoring workshop with industrial sewing machines and design tools","Professional electrical installation training bay with safe practice environments","Carpentry workshop with hand and power tools for practical training","Masonry and concrete training yard for bricklaying practice","Welding bay with arc and gas welding stations","Plumbing workshop with various pipe systems and fixtures","Automotive mechanics bay with diagnostic equipment and vehicle lifts","Library with reference materials and computers for research","Student commons and recreational facilities","Convenient private rental housing options around PIM Trading Centre for non-local learners"]},jh=[{number:"01",title:"Choose Your Course",description:"Explore available programmes and select the course that matches your interests."},{number:"02",title:"Complete Your Application",description:"Submit your application online through our secure form."},{number:"03",title:"Application Review",description:"Your application will be reviewed by the admissions team."},{number:"04",title:"Begin Your Journey",description:"Receive admission information and prepare to join Aida Chilembwe CTC."}],Wy=[{value:"8",suffix:"+",label:"Accredited Trades"},{value:"100",suffix:"%",label:"Hands-on Workshop"},{value:"2027",label:"Upcoming Intake"},{value:"100",suffix:"%",label:"TEVETA Aligned"}],hi=[{label:"Home",href:"/"},{label:"About",href:"/#about"},{label:"Admissions",href:"/#admissions"},{label:"Contact",href:"/#contact"}],wh=[{label:"Academics",links:[{label:"All Courses",href:"/courses"},{label:"Timetable",href:"/timetable"},{label:"Fees & Tuition",href:"/#fees"}]},{label:"Campus & News",links:[{label:"Announcements",href:"/announcements"},{label:"Campus Life & Gallery",href:"/#gallery"},{label:"Ask Admissions",href:"/ask-question"}]}],$y=["Information & Communication Technology","Electrical Installation & Electronics","Automobile Mechanics","Fabrication & Welding","Plumbing","Carpentry & Joinery","Bricklaying","Tailoring & Fashion Designing"],va={tuitionGovernmentPerTerm:5e4,tuitionParallelPerTerm:15e4,parallelOnlyCourseIds:["automobile"],studentsUnionOneOff:5e3,registrationOneOff:1e4,bankAccounts:[{id:"government",title:"Government Sponsored Students",note:"NOTE: ALL GOVERNMENT SPONSORED STUDENTS SHOULD DEPOSIT INSTITUTION FEES TO THE FOLLOWING ACCOUNT DETAIL",accountName:"AIDA CHILEMBWE COMMUNITY TECHNICAL COLLEGE",bankName:"FDH (FIRST DISCOUNT BANK)",serviceCentre:"CHIRADZULU",accountNumber:"1130000074057",instructions:"REMEMBER TO BRING DEPOSIT SLIP TO THE BURSAR."},{id:"parallel",title:"Parallel Sponsored Students",note:"NOTE: ALL PARALLEL SPONSORED STUDENTS SHOULD DEPOSIT INSTITUTION FEES TO THE FOLLOWING ACCOUNT DETAIL",accountName:"AIDA CHILEMBWE COMMUNITY TECHNICAL COLLEGE",bankName:"FDH (FIRST DISCOUNT BANK)",serviceCentre:"CHIRADZULU",accountNumber:"1130000076699",instructions:"REMEMBER TO BRING DEPOSIT SLIP TO THE BURSAR."}]},Nh=[{id:"g1",title:"ICT Network & Programming Lab",category:"Workshops",image:"/images/courses/ict.jpg",caption:"Modern computing lab equipped with networking racks, dual displays and software tools."},{id:"g2",title:"Electrical Training & Installation Bay",category:"Workshops",image:"/images/courses/electrical.jpg",caption:"Students master commercial switchboards, domestic wiring conduits, and solar circuit panels."},{id:"g3",title:"Automotive Mechanics Inspection",category:"Workshops",image:"/images/courses/automobile.jpg",caption:"Engine diagnostic bay featuring electronic scanners, transmission jacks, and vehicle lift bays."},{id:"g4",title:"Metal Fabrication & Arc Welding",category:"Workshops",image:"/images/courses/welding.jpg",caption:"Heavy-duty steel fabrication, oxy-acetylene torch cutting, and precision arc welding stations."},{id:"g5",title:"Tailoring & Pattern Drafting Studio",category:"Student Projects",image:"/images/courses/tailoring.jpg",caption:"Garment design, pattern grading, and high-speed industrial stitching workstations."},{id:"g6",title:"Carpentry & Bespoke Joinery Workshop",category:"Workshops",image:"/images/courses/carpentry.jpg",caption:"Timber seasoning, wood turning lathes, mortise and tenon craftsmanship for furniture creation."},{id:"g7",title:"Masonry & Structural Bricklaying Yard",category:"Student Projects",image:"/images/courses/bricklaying.jpg",caption:"Outdoor construction testing area for laying certified brick foundations and structural lintels."},{id:"g8",title:"Graduation & Academic Achievement",category:"Ceremonies",image:"/images/tendai.jpg",caption:"Proud technical graduates receiving national trade accreditation credentials."},{id:"g9",title:"Student Community & Fellowship",category:"Campus Life",image:"/images/anthuinu.jpg",caption:"Inclusive student body collaborating on technical projects in historic Chiradzulu."}],kc=[{id:"office-1",raw:"265881980643",formatted:"+265 (0) 881 980 643"},{id:"office-2",raw:"265882913047",formatted:"+265 (0) 882 913 047"},{id:"office-3",raw:"265881080653",formatted:"+265 (0) 881 080 653"},{id:"admissions-enquiries",raw:"265884560048",formatted:"+265 (0) 884 560 048"}],Fy="265884560048",Py="bdarlingtone@gmail.com",ue={name:"Aida Chilembwe Community Technical College",shortName:"Aida Chilembwe CTC",intake:"2027",applicationUrl:"h